{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringLatticeSpanFiniteQuotient","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringLatticeSpanFiniteQuotient","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.OrderOfElement","lean:module:QOU.BringLatticeSpan"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.bring_left_mul_scalar_of_hom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.bring_left_mul_scalar_of_hom","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpanFiniteQuotient.lean#L93-L107","doc":"**`bring_left_mul_scalar` via a finite quotient.** Under the hypotheses of\n`bring_span_eq_top_of_hom`, a left multiplication `L_v` commuting with every element of `S`\nis a scalar. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.bring_span_eq_top_of_hom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.bring_span_eq_top_of_hom","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpanFiniteQuotient.lean#L77-L91","doc":"**Bring's triangle group spans, via a finite quotient.** As `bring_span_eq_top`, with `hS`\nreplaced by: a monoid hom `ρ` from the monoid generated by `s, u` to a finite group `G`, whose\nkernel lies in `S`. Kattan–Singerman's definition of Bring's group (kernel of\n`Δ(2,5,4) → S₅`, lifted to `SL(2)`) supplies such a `ρ` with `G = S₅`; that map is cited,\nnot constructed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.exists_pow_succ_mem_of_hom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.exists_pow_succ_mem_of_hom","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpanFiniteQuotient.lean#L60-L69","doc":"**Submonoid version.** `T` a submonoid of an ambient monoid `A`, `ρ : T →* G` with `G` a\nfinite group, and every `g ∈ T` with `ρ g = 1` lying in `S ⊆ A`. Then every element of `T`\nhas a positive power in `S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.exists_pow_succ_mem_of_mker_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.exists_pow_succ_mem_of_mker_le","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpanFiniteQuotient.lean#L48-L58","doc":"**Positive powers land in any submonoid containing the kernel of a hom to a finite\ngroup.** For `ρ : M →* G` with `G` a finite group and `ρ.mker ≤ S`, every `g : M` has a\npositive power in `S`, namely `g ^ Nat.card G`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}